    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2">

                <pb facs="0011" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg1"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt and
                        Prime Minister Churchill to Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek
                    </hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d2-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Casablanca</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-25">January 25, 1943</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>We have been meeting in North Africa with our Chiefs of Staff,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d2-f2"/> to plan our offensives and strategy for 1943. The vital
                    importance of aiding China has filled our minds. General Arnold, the Commander
                    of the U. S. Air Force, is already on his way to see you. We have decided that
                        Chennault<anchor n="4" xml:id="d2-f3"/> should be reinforced at once in
                    order that you may strike not only at vital shipping routes but at Japan
                    herself. Arnold carries to you our best judgment as to Burma. He will also
                    advise you about our expanding operations in the South West Pacific <pb
                        facs="0012" n="2" xml:id="pg2"/> and our developing offensive against
                    Germany and Italy which will follow promptly after the destruction of the Axis
                    forces in Tunisia. We have great confidence in the 1943 offensives of the United
                    Nations and want to assure you that we intend with your co-operation to keep the
                    pressure on Japan at an ever increasing tempo.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d2-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d2-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of telegram obtained from the Franklin D. Roosevelt Library, Hyde Park, New
                    York Notation at end of text: “O.K. F.D.R. I concur. W.S.C.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d2-f2" n="3" xml:id="d2-f2-content">
                <p>The records of the Casablanca Conference are scheduled for publication in a
                    subsequent volume of <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d2-f3" n="4" xml:id="d2-f3-content">
                <p>Brig. Gen. Claire L. Chennault, commanding United States Air Task Force in
                    China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
